      {
        "id": 211611,
        "name": "Princess Cool",
        "username": "Princess_Cool",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/p/34f0e0/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2017-12-28T02:29:54.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"The Burning Stickman\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n The Burning Stickman:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>Princess Cool wrote:</b><br><blockquote>I'm definitely making Fashion in the RPG, I already had a similar idea that just needs some small alterations.\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nWill she be 'Classic' Fashion, or Fashion hardened and brutal after her experiences in the Colliseum?You know, stories like that always have me thinking about the people left behind -- Shirley had friends and family and allies among the heroes. It must have hit them pretty hard that she was basically kidnapped into that kind of brutal slavery.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Classic Fashion, she'll go into battle in a full sequined ballgown to dazzle her enemies with oppulence.&nbsp;</p>",
