      {
        "id": 211612,
        "name": "Trajector",
        "username": "Trajector",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/trajector/{size}/1914_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-12-30T02:22:29.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Ehkrickor\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ehkrickor/48/2035_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Ehkrickor:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<div><b>Jeysie wrote:</b><br>\n<blockquote>It also reminds me of Hedy Lamarr, who was a talented inventor in addition to being a beautiful actress.Also, I feel like your Cult should get in touch with Argent; dude clearly has a flair for causing fear and nightmares in extreme circumstances. \n</blockquote>\n</div>\n<p>“What are you Worried about Heddy? It’s 1884 You’ll be able to sue HER! ahaha” ~ Governor WIlliam J. Lepetomane</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>It’s <span class=\"bbcode-i\">Hedley.</span></p>\n<p>Is anybody else getting more and more put off by the Argent Adept as we learn more about his abilities? He seems to be WAY overpowered as a single combatant with abilities that do WAY too much at once, especially given how supporty, plinky, and self-comboy his deck is.</p>",
