        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arcanist_lupus/{size}/2169_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-12-30T20:13:16.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Trajector\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/trajector/48/1914_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Trajector:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<div><b>Jeysie wrote:</b><br>\n<blockquote>\nSo both Legacy and Argent hold back their abilities to leading and supporting their allies, because we've seen they both have the sort of personality who prefers to handle things in less-lethal ways where they can. And much like Iron Legacy was absolutely terrifying when he felt like he had his back put against the wall, so is Argent.\n</blockquote>\n</div>\n<p>This argument would make sense to me if his deck gave him lots of different situational special abilities. Things like making targets unable to deal damage, putting cards in play back into their decks, redirecting damage, making a hero’s damage irreducible, making decks unable to play cards, and whatnot. Then, I could easily imagine that if he unleashed his magical abilities, he’d be able to do all the things we see him doing in the lore. I’m just thinking that, based on his deck alone, it seems like if he unleashed his abilities he’d be able to put +1 damage on ALL hero targets instead of just TWO.</p>\n<p>I kind of agree about Fanatic, too, but in her case, at least her deck has Wrathful Retribution and a couple other big-slam power cards - even if they are spaced out by plinky or more situational cards. In her case, I guess her deck represents Fanatic when she’s not yet embraced her full power. And her Prime Wardens variant adds a whole lot of power to her play. Argent Adept, on the other hand, has variants that basically just change the way he activates his Ongoing and support abilities.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Maybe he starts using Sarabande of Destruction against villain targets?</p>",
        "post_number": 28,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:42:13.005Z",
