        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jeysie/{size}/1868_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-12-30T20:22:16.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>@<a href=\"https://greaterthangames.com/users/trajector\" title=\"View user profile.\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">Trajector</a>:&nbsp;I admit I thought you meant working from a storytelling standpoint.</p><p>Because C&amp;A have said on a number of occasions that everyone's deck is just a snapshot of their abilities that makes sense both for that specific point in time and for gameplay purposes. IIRC they specifically said in Argent's podcast he can \"do pretty much anything with Void energy\" and so his deck is necessarily limited.</p><p>(I admit to being rather interested at this point in both Tactics and the RPG re: Argent and Virtuoso characters in general.)</p>",
