      {
        "id": 211620,
        "name": "FrivYeti",
        "username": "FrivYeti",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/frivyeti/{size}/1919_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-01-08T18:20:51.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I dunno, this is right up the alley of the Adept. He gets Combo-absurd:</p><p>1. Silver Shadow lets you activate an accompany; use Alacritous Subdominant to trigger Xu's Bell for +1 Damage, then get another power use off your second Subdominant.&nbsp;</p><p>2. Your second power use goes to the Lyre, which blows up Xu's Bell to kill a Gladiator and then hits Gladiator #2 for 2 damage.</p><p>3. You still have a card play. Play Silver Shadow. Hit Gladiator #2 for 2 damage. Then play Polyphoric Flare. Deal yourself 3 damage, and then use that power use to trigger the Harp, killing Gladiation #3 and hitting Gladiator #2 for another 2 damage (total 6, possibly killing them).</p><p>4. You still have a power use. Use it on the Pipes to trigger both your Melodies of Frost and Flame, hitting one gladiator for 8 damage and killing them.&nbsp;</p><p>That's four gladiators out in one go.</p>",
